## The accepted deviations (orchestrator, 2026-11-18)

The orchestrator accepted both deviations, and the third edit, after the first look:

1. `detail` 0.0035 changed to 0.0025. The sharp rim edge facets showed at 4x zoom without it.
2. The ellipsoid clip and the flat bottom cut take a 0.005 m smooth roll (`smoothIntersect`). The
   gate needs this: cutout-check.mjs reports a dark halo when the rim edge is a sharp coin edge.
   First count: 308 of 885 edge pixels on the red front, worst drop 71 %. After the rim roll only
   the yellow three-quarter failed, on 89 of 796 edge pixels (10 % is the limit).
3. The flat bottom cut takes the same 0.005 m roll. This cleared the last 89 pixels. The flat
   contact stays: the bottom face is flat over the middle, and stats.json gives bottomY -0.001 m.

The roll lowers the measured centre thickness from 0.033 m to 0.0326 m. The lens keeps the order's
values (0.23 m radius, 0.0165 m half thickness).

